course: dictionary
lesson: 13987
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and logging is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. These are the context clues. «The team is logging the rainfall every morning.» Here logging means writing down information, because the team is recording the rain.
explain: «Logging in takes seconds when you remember your password.» Here logging in means entering your name and password to start using a computer or website. The little word in tells you which meaning is needed.
explain: «Logging in the rainforest has cut down many old trees.» Here logging means cutting down trees and taking the wood away to sell. Ask yourself: what is happening in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Logging means cutting down trees and taking the wood away to sell.
fact: Logging can also mean writing down information in a log or record, such as «logging the weather each day».
fact: Logging in means entering your name and password to start using a computer or website. Logging out means leaving it.
fact: Logging of rainforests can harm the animals that live there, because they lose their homes.
fact: Context clues, such as the words after logging, tell you which meaning is right.
exercise: «Logging in the rainforest has cut down many trees.» What does logging mean here? | Walking along a forest trail | *Cutting down trees and taking the wood away | Entering a password to use a computer | Writing down information in a log
exercise: «Every morning we are logging the temperature in a table.» What does logging mean here? | *Writing down information in a record | Leaving a website | Splashing in a river | Cutting down trees to sell
exercise: «Before you can use the school computer, you need to start logging in with your password.» What does logging in mean? | Cutting wood to sell | Shutting the computer down for the night | Writing the date in a diary | *Entering your name and password to start using it
test: «When she finished her work, she was logging out of the website.» What does logging out mean? | *Leaving the website | Writing about the website in a log | Starting a new website | Choosing a new password
test: «The data logger is logging the light level every hour.» What is the logger doing? | Drawing a picture of the light | Cutting down trees | Locking the door | *Recording information over time
exam: «Logging is harming the rainforest and the animals that live there.» What does logging mean in this sentence? | *Cutting down trees and taking the wood away | Counting the animals in the forest | Entering a password to start a computer | Writing information in a record
